From: Pehacorp Kernel Optimization <kernel@pehacorp.local>
Date: Sun, 02 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7921: fix self-deadlock on 6 GHz association

mt7921_mac_sta_add() runs under dev->mt76.mutex, taken by the mac80211
core in mt76_sta_add() before calling into the driver's ->sta_add().
It calls mt7921_regd_set_6ghz_power_type(), which -- whenever the vif's
operating channel is in the 6 GHz band -- calls mt7921_mcu_regd_update(),
which itself does mt792x_mutex_acquire(dev), i.e. tries to take the same
dev->mt76.mutex again. mutex_lock() is not recursive, so this is a
guaranteed self-deadlock the moment a vif associates on a 6 GHz BSS,
hanging wpa_supplicant and taking the whole network stack down with it
(observed as "task wpa_supplicant is blocked on a mutex likely owned by
task wpa_supplicant" in dmesg, confirmed via journalctl on 2026-08-02
across two separate rc5 boots, both hanging within minutes of roaming
onto our AP's 6 GHz BSSID).

This whole CLC/6GHz-power-type call chain is new in the 7.2-rc5 tree
(regd.c does not exist in our 7.1.5 tree at all), so 7.1.5 is unaffected.

Fix: split mt7921_mcu_regd_update() into the actual work
(mt7921_mcu_regd_update_locked(), assumes the caller already holds
dev->mt76.mutex) and a thin wrapper that takes the mutex before calling
it. mt7921_regd_set_6ghz_power_type() -- always called from a sta_add/
sta_remove path that already holds the mutex -- now calls the _locked
variant directly instead of re-entering the wrapper.

NOTE (check at 7.2 final release): this is a workaround for a bug in
code that was still moving during the rc cycle. Before re-applying this
patch to a new source drop, re-check whether mt7921_mac_sta_add() /
mt7921_regd_set_6ghz_power_type() / mt7921_mcu_regd_update() still have
this shape -- if upstream restructured or fixed the locking, this patch
may no longer apply, or worse, may no longer be needed.

Signed-off-by: Pehacorp Kernel Optimization <kernel@pehacorp.local>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7921/regd.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7921/regd.c
@@ -71,35 +71,39 @@
 	}
 }

-int mt7921_mcu_regd_update(struct mt792x_dev *dev, u8 *alpha2,
-			   enum environment_cap country_ie_env)
+int mt7921_mcu_regd_update_locked(struct mt792x_dev *dev, u8 *alpha2,
+				  enum environment_cap country_ie_env)
 {
 	struct mt76_dev *mdev = &dev->mt76;
 	struct ieee80211_hw *hw = mdev->hw;
 	struct wiphy *wiphy = hw->wiphy;
 	int ret = 0;

-	dev->regd_in_progress = true;
-
-	mt792x_mutex_acquire(dev);
 	if (!dev->regd_change)
-		goto err;
+		return 0;

 	ret = mt7921_mcu_set_clc(dev, alpha2, country_ie_env);
 	if (ret < 0)
-		goto err;
+		return ret;

 	mt7921_regd_channel_update(wiphy, dev);

 	ret = mt76_connac_mcu_set_channel_domain(hw->priv);
 	if (ret < 0)
-		goto err;
+		return ret;

-	ret = mt7921_set_tx_sar_pwr(hw, NULL);
-	if (ret < 0)
-		goto err;
+	return mt7921_set_tx_sar_pwr(hw, NULL);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(mt7921_mcu_regd_update_locked);

-err:
+int mt7921_mcu_regd_update(struct mt792x_dev *dev, u8 *alpha2,
+			   enum environment_cap country_ie_env)
+{
+	int ret;
+
+	dev->regd_in_progress = true;
+	mt792x_mutex_acquire(dev);
+	ret = mt7921_mcu_regd_update_locked(dev, alpha2, country_ie_env);
 	mt792x_mutex_release(dev);
 	dev->regd_change = false;
 	dev->regd_in_progress = false;
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7921/regd.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7921/regd.h
@@ -8,6 +8,8 @@
 struct wiphy;
 struct regulatory_request;

+int mt7921_mcu_regd_update_locked(struct mt792x_dev *dev, u8 *alpha2,
+				  enum environment_cap country_ie_env);
 int mt7921_mcu_regd_update(struct mt792x_dev *dev, u8 *alpha2,
 			   enum environment_cap country_ie_env);
 void mt7921_regd_notifier(struct wiphy *wiphy,
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7921/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt76/mt7921/main.c
@@ -802,7 +802,11 @@

 out:
 	if (vif->bss_conf.chanreq.oper.chan->band == NL80211_BAND_6GHZ)
-		mt7921_mcu_regd_update(dev, dev->mt76.alpha2, dev->country_ie_env);
+		/* Called from mt7921_mac_sta_add()/_remove(), which already run
+		 * under dev->mt76.mutex (taken by mt76_sta_add()/_remove()) --
+		 * use the pre-locked variant to avoid re-entering the mutex.
+		 */
+		mt7921_mcu_regd_update_locked(dev, dev->mt76.alpha2, dev->country_ie_env);
 }

 int mt7921_mac_sta_add(struct mt76_dev *mdev, struct ieee80211_vif *vif,
